From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 7778777 <7778777@7778777.online>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:19:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] vm: copy pages being laundered instead of stealing them

vm_pageout_setup wires a page that goes to the default memory manager,
and the manager's map wires it again, since the manager wires its whole
address space (vm_wire_all).  When the manager sends such a page on with
the deallocate bit, vm_map_copyin_page_list tries to steal a page that
is wired twice:

  vm_map_copyin_page_list: Assertion `m->wire_count == 1' failed.

Without assertions the page is stolen with its laundry bit still set,
and vm_page_laundry_count is never decremented for it.

mach-defpager does this when a file of a tmpfs is truncated to a size
that is not a multiple of the page size, and the last page is resident
and dirty: it clears the end of the returned page and supplies it again.

* vm/vm_map.c (vm_map_copyin_page_list): Do not steal a page whose
laundry bit is set; it is copied, and vm_map_delete frees the original.
---
 vm/vm_map.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vm/vm_map.c b/vm/vm_map.c
index a0f98702..7be3c84d 100644
--- a/vm/vm_map.c
+++ b/vm/vm_map.c
@@ -4347,6 +4347,7 @@ retry:
 			 *	      the object is temporary, and
 			 *	      not shared.
 			 *	(2) The page is not precious.
+			 *	(3) The page is not being laundered.
 			 *
 			 *	The not shared check consists of two
 			 *	parts:  (a) there are no objects that
@@ -4362,6 +4363,13 @@ retry:
 			 *	Stealing wired pages requires telling the
 			 *	pmap module to let go of them.
 			 *
+			 *	A page being laundered was wired by
+			 *	vm_pageout_setup, on top of the wiring of
+			 *	the default memory manager's map, and stays
+			 *	so until the manager frees it.  Such a page
+			 *	is copied, and vm_map_delete then frees the
+			 *	original like any other.
+			 *
 			 *	NOTE: stealing clean pages from objects
 			 *  	whose mappings survive requires a call to
 			 *	the pmap module.  Maybe later.
@@ -4374,7 +4382,8 @@ retry:
 			    src_object->temporary &&
 			    (!src_object->shadowed) &&
 			    (!src_object->use_shared_copy) &&
-			    !m->precious) {
+			    !m->precious &&
+			    !m->laundry) {
 				vm_offset_t	page_vaddr;
 
 				page_vaddr = src_start + (i * PAGE_SIZE);
